Usage: see SET COLORIZE_NICKS, COLORIZE_CHANNELS, COLORIZE_WARP
  ScrollZ can colour nicknames and channel names automatically.
  Every name is given a colour computed from the name itself, so a
  given nick or channel always appears in the same colour - across
  every window, every message type and every session. This makes it
  easier to follow who is talking and which channel a line came
  from, without any manual colour setup.

  The feature is controlled entirely through SET variables:

    SET COLORIZE_NICKS ON|OFF      colour nicknames     (default ON)
    SET COLORIZE_CHANNELS ON|OFF   colour channel names (default ON)
    SET COLORIZE_WARP <number>     reshuffle the colours (default 0)

  Colours come from a fixed palette chosen for legibility on dark
  terminals, and only the name itself is wrapped -
  mIRC colour codes and the rest of the line are left untouched.

  Colours are only shown when SET DISPLAY_ANSI is ON. This automatic
  colouring is separate from the COLOR command, which sets the fixed
  colours used for event types such as joins and kicks.

See Also:
  SET COLORIZE_NICKS
  SET COLORIZE_CHANNELS
  SET COLORIZE_WARP
  SET DISPLAY_ANSI
  COLOR
